1
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,039
Are you alright?

2
00:00:09,599 --> 00:00:10,400
I'm fine.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,800
Sit.

4
00:00:18,359 --> 00:00:19,800
So why did Song Cheng show up?

5
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:21,600
Does she know about our plan?

6
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,199
I don't know.

7
00:00:25,719 --> 00:00:26,679
But she

8
00:00:27,879 --> 00:00:28,719
doesn't seem to care.

9
00:00:29,239 --> 00:00:31,760
Figured out what you're
going to tell Song Huan tomorrow?

10
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,159
Song Huan has had a firm foothold
in Song Group for years.

11
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,759
Going up against her now

12
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:40,960
would be fighting a losing battle.

13
00:00:49,359 --> 00:00:50,159
What?

14
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,399
Do you think

15
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,399
I'm being too cruel to Song Cheng?

16
00:00:56,039 --> 00:00:56,840
Song,

17
00:00:58,719 --> 00:00:59,640
I'll say it again.

18
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,200
Whatever you decide,

19
00:01:02,439 --> 00:01:03,359
I'm with you.

20
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:07,920
=Dear Song=

21
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:10,613
=Episode 14=
(Falling Out)

22
00:01:22,519 --> 00:01:23,560
Ms. Song Huan.

23
00:01:24,719 --> 00:01:25,959
I'd like to talk to you.

24
00:02:05,599 --> 00:02:06,239
Ms. Song Huan,

25
00:02:06,239 --> 00:02:07,840
do you like any of these new pieces?

26
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,159
Help me pick.

27
00:02:19,759 --> 00:02:21,120
All of them suit you

28
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,400
except the third one.

29
00:02:24,759 --> 00:02:25,560
Why?

30
00:02:25,919 --> 00:02:28,639
The third dress
is your favorite shade of red,

31
00:02:28,719 --> 00:02:31,240
but it's embroidered with wild roses.

32
00:02:31,719 --> 00:02:32,719
Wild roses have small blooms

33
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:33,719
and a short flowering season.

34
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:36,000
They don't suit you nearly as well
as roses that bloom all year.

35
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,599
Do as she says.

36
00:02:38,319 --> 00:02:39,319
Send everything

37
00:02:39,319 --> 00:02:40,520
except the third one to the Song house.

38
00:02:40,719 --> 00:02:41,919
Yes, Ms. Song Huan.

39
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,960
Wrap up the third one for her.

40
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,439
But these dresses

41
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,719
are all made to your measurements.

42
00:02:52,039 --> 00:02:54,439
Then let's get another one custom-made.

43
00:02:57,039 --> 00:02:58,120
I'll measure her myself.

44
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,800
This dress is so expensive.

45
00:03:13,919 --> 00:03:14,719
I can't accept it.

46
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,520
Wild roses bloom briefly,

47
00:03:18,759 --> 00:03:20,120
but they've got plenty of ambition.

48
00:03:21,719 --> 00:03:23,759
They can take root in any open field.

49
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,199
It suits you.

50
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,719
So what did you ask me out here

51
00:03:28,719 --> 00:03:30,360
to talk about?

52
00:03:32,599 --> 00:03:34,719
Just being able to work for you

53
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,560
is already enough for me.

54
00:03:42,759 --> 00:03:44,560
You know what I like about you?

55
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,400
You've got guts.

56
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,960
You want to be a knockoff of me.

57
00:03:55,759 --> 00:03:56,840
Ms. Song Huan.

58
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:01,240
You don't mind me imitating you?

59
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:07,319
In this world,

60
00:04:07,759 --> 00:04:09,719
a knockoff can never outshine
the original.

61
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,399
Yu Song?

62
00:04:50,319 --> 00:04:51,720
When did you come in?

63
00:04:52,519 --> 00:04:53,120
Just now.

64
00:04:53,439 --> 00:04:54,720
I saw you were asleep,

65
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,000
so I thought I'd move the wooden horse

66
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,120
to keep it from pressing on your arm.

67
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,600
I guess staying up late these past
two nights polishing it wore me out.

68
00:05:03,439 --> 00:05:04,000
Look.

69
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,519
I did it.

70
00:05:05,759 --> 00:05:06,480
You think

71
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,120
Mr. Yu will like it?

72
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,120
It looks so lifelike.

73
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,720
Mr. Yu will definitely like it.

74
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:20,920
Oh, Yu Song,

75
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,319
can you help me get it wrapped?

76
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:25,399
I don't trust anyone else

77
00:05:25,399 --> 00:05:26,519
but you.

78
00:05:26,759 --> 00:05:28,759
Bring it to the venue for me tomorrow.

79
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,639
(Pour this on the wooden horse.)

80
00:06:30,519 --> 00:06:31,480
Mr. Yu,

81
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,260
is there anything else
you'd like me to improve?

82
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:36,160
Reinforce this part.

83
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:36,959
Then

84
00:06:37,279 --> 00:06:39,160
see if it's worth
developing this side too.

85
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:41,040
We'll be developing it soon.

86
00:06:41,319 --> 00:06:42,720
- Pleasure working with you.
- Pleasure working with you.

87
00:06:48,639 --> 00:06:49,519
I'm really looking forward

88
00:06:49,519 --> 00:06:51,040
to Ms. Song Cheng's gift.

89
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:53,560
Mr. Yu.

90
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:54,720
Just a small token.

91
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,000
Hope you like it.

92
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:56,920
Hmm.

93
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,319
Ms. Song Cheng, it's thoughtful of you.

94
00:07:43,439 --> 00:07:44,240
Mr. Yu.

95
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:45,759
We never expected

96
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,639
something like this to happen.

97
00:07:48,399 --> 00:07:49,519
Sorry to give you a scare.

98
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:50,720
Cheng,

99
00:07:51,639 --> 00:07:52,720
what exactly happened?

100
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,920
Dad.

101
00:07:54,959 --> 00:07:56,720
I really don't know what happened.

102
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,040
Forget it.

103
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:00,360
Ah.

104
00:08:00,639 --> 00:08:01,800
Accidents happen.

105
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:03,199
But

106
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,120
I don't think it's a good sign.

107
00:08:15,439 --> 00:08:16,519
Ms. Song Huan,

108
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:19,399
this is the gift you asked me
to hold onto for you.

109
00:08:28,199 --> 00:08:30,079
Hope this gift from Song Group

110
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,519
is a nice surprise,

111
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,200
not a shock.

112
00:08:53,559 --> 00:08:54,480
Good.

113
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,320
Two horses sharing one pearl. Great.

114
00:08:56,759 --> 00:08:58,320
Mr. Song,
you really put thought into this.

115
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,039
You've got a great daughter.

116
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:03,799
I'm glad you like it, Mr. Yu.

117
00:09:04,519 --> 00:09:05,559
Then Song Huan will handle

118
00:09:05,919 --> 00:09:07,639
the rest of the project with you.

119
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:08,879
Alright.

120
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,720
Rest assured, Mr. Yu.

121
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,200
Don't worry, Dad.

122
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,080
Song Cheng's work has been put on hold.

123
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:23,799
I'm now the one coordinating

124
00:09:23,799 --> 00:09:24,960
with Yu Qixian.

125
00:09:27,039 --> 00:09:28,919
Your idea of carving the two horses

126
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,320
was a good call.

127
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,639
"Two Horses Playing with a Pearl"

128
00:09:32,639 --> 00:09:34,240
represents the Song and Yu families,

129
00:09:34,639 --> 00:09:36,320
and also you and Song Cheng.

130
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:38,840
That way,
Mr. Song won't blame this accident

131
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,279
on you.

132
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,320
You really planned out every step.

133
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:43,799
I just thought

134
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,320
a few steps ahead for you.

135
00:09:47,279 --> 00:09:48,679
But I'm curious.

136
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:50,840
For this accident,

137
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,960
why didn't you use

138
00:09:54,759 --> 00:09:56,720
the concentrated sulfuric acid
I prepared for you?

139
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,320
Destroying the target directly

140
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,879
is the easiest way,

141
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,039
but it's also the most likely
to leave traces.

142
00:10:08,559 --> 00:10:09,679
And the effect

143
00:10:09,679 --> 00:10:12,240
wouldn't be nearly as damaging
as destroying it on the spot.

144
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:15,080
Go on.

145
00:10:15,759 --> 00:10:17,720
I prepared two identical wooden boxes.

146
00:10:18,039 --> 00:10:19,440
I coated the hidden compartment

147
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:21,240
of that box with nitrate powder.

148
00:10:21,519 --> 00:10:22,480
That wooden horse

149
00:10:22,559 --> 00:10:25,720
was a fake carved
from cheap pine soaked in oil.

150
00:10:25,919 --> 00:10:27,720
Nitrate is a strong oxidizer.

151
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:30,240
When the box opens, the powder
is exposed to plenty of oxygen.

152
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:31,879
The oil-soaked wood then flares up.

153
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:33,720
Thick smoke, a burnt smell,

154
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,480
and a piece of wood
burned beyond recognition

155
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,080
were enough to cause a scare.

156
00:10:46,559 --> 00:10:47,799
I've always seen you

157
00:10:48,639 --> 00:10:50,039
as a knockoff of me.

158
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,320
But sometimes I think

159
00:10:54,039 --> 00:10:55,159
you're even more ruthless than me.

160
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,559
That way,

161
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:01,639
Song Cheng is in for a rough time.

162
00:11:02,039 --> 00:11:03,039
And Song Huaishan

163
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,240
will no longer hold out hope for her.

164
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:12,639
You really don't care?

165
00:11:14,919 --> 00:11:16,440
Like I said from the start,

166
00:11:17,039 --> 00:11:18,360
you're the one I want to follow,

167
00:11:18,559 --> 00:11:19,919
Ms. Song Huan.

168
00:11:24,039 --> 00:11:26,039
I've been looking
for a personal assistant.

169
00:11:28,039 --> 00:11:29,120
This employee card

170
00:11:30,159 --> 00:11:32,320
gives you access privileges
second only to senior management.

171
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,240
Thanks, Ms. Song Huan.

172
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,240
Tonight's reception

173
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,159
isn't some game of romance.

174
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,840
A couture gown

175
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,720
is the bare minimum for getting in.

176
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:50,600
Got it,

177
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:51,519
Ms. Song Huan.

178
00:12:17,039 --> 00:12:18,759
(Wild roses are untamed)

179
00:12:18,759 --> 00:12:20,759
(and grow unchecked,)

180
00:12:20,759 --> 00:12:23,279
(taking over space from other plants,)

181
00:12:23,639 --> 00:12:24,840
(including roses.)
